TITLE = "Predicting Customer Churn in Subscription Services Using Interpretable Machine Learning"
SUBTITLE = "A Business Decision-Support Framework for Retention Management"
AUTHOR = "Steven Eleojo Onoja"
AFFIL = ["School of Computing", "Ulster University", "Belfast, United Kingdom", "onoja-se@ulster.ac.uk"]

ABSTRACT = ("Abstract—Customer churn erodes the recurring revenue on which subscription businesses depend, yet the machine learning models that predict churn most "
"accurately are often the ones business users understand least. This paper presents and evaluates a framework that treats predictive accuracy and interpretability as "
"joint design objectives rather than competing ones. Logistic regression, random forest, and gradient-boosted trees are trained under a single seven-stage protocol on "
"two public datasets drawn from different sectors, retail banking and subscription streaming, and each model is assessed on two axes: discrimination and calibration on "
"one, and the stability and fidelity of the explanations it supports on the other. Shapley attributions are computed for every scored customer and audited against local "
"surrogate explanations on a stratified sample of one hundred records per model. On the banking data, gradient boosting improves the Matthews correlation coefficient by "
"0.102 over the transparent baseline while agreement between the two explainers falls by 0.176 and rank agreement by 0.420, which quantifies a cost of opacity that the "
"literature more often asserts than measures. Attributions are mapped through an editable retention intervention taxonomy that converts statistical drivers into "
"prioritised, customer-specific actions with named business owners, and are delivered through a dashboard built for non-technical customer relationship management staff. "
"A fairness audit of the recommended banking model returns selection-rate ratios of 0.50, 0.36, and 0.07 across gender, country, and age band, all below the four-fifths "
"convention; the decision layer therefore explains demographic drivers but never acts on them. Ethical safeguards covering data privacy, fairness, and human oversight "
"are built into the implementation rather than appended to it.")

KEYWORDS = ("Keywords—customer churn; interpretable machine learning; explainable artificial intelligence; decision-support systems; customer retention; Shapley values")

# item types: h1, h2, h5, body, bullet, eq, table, fig, figwide
CONTENT = [
("h1","Introduction"),
("body","Subscription businesses live or die by their ability to keep the customers they already have. Customer churn, understood here as the voluntary decision of a "
"subscriber to terminate a service relationship, is among the most closely watched indicators in telecommunications, banking, software-as-a-service, and electronic "
"commerce, because the economics of retention and acquisition are sharply asymmetric. Acquiring a new customer typically costs several times more than retaining an "
"existing one, and modest improvements in retention compound into disproportionately large gains in customer lifetime value {{hadden,verbeke}}. Lemmens and Gupta "
"estimate that firms which target retention campaigns using loss-aware models can improve campaign profit substantially relative to conventional targeting, which "
"suggests that the value of churn modelling lies less in the prediction itself than in the decisions the prediction informs {{lemmens}}."),
("body","Machine learning (ML) has become the standard technical response to the churn problem. Comparative studies report that ensemble methods, particularly random "
"forests and gradient-boosted decision trees, outperform simpler classifiers on the benchmark datasets used in this literature {{vafeiadis,ahmad}}. Yet accuracy "
"gains of this kind have not translated into equally widespread operational adoption. A retention manager who is told only that a customer has a churn probability "
"of 0.82 has no basis for choosing between a price concession, a service upgrade, or a support call, and no way to judge whether the model's reasoning is sound. "
"Rudin has argued forcefully that opaque models are routinely deployed in settings where the cost of an unexplained error is high, and that the absence of "
"interpretability is a deployment risk rather than a cosmetic shortcoming {{rudin}}. In regulated sectors the concern is sharper still, since European data "
"protection rules give individuals a qualified right to meaningful information about automated decisions that affect them {{goodman}}."),
("body","Explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) offers a route out of this impasse. Post-hoc attribution methods such as SHapley Additive exPlanations (SHAP) and "
"Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations (LIME) attach a quantified contribution to every input feature of every individual prediction {{lundberg,ribeiro}}. "
"A growing number of churn studies now include such explanations {{elattar}}. What these studies generally do not include is the final step that retention practice "
"requires: a systematic translation of explanation outputs into concrete retention actions that a non-technical customer relationship management (CRM) team can "
"execute and audit. Explanations are produced for the data scientist and stop at the data scientist."),
("body","This paper presents an interpretable churn prediction framework in which the explanation layer is designed from the outset as the input to a business "
"decision-support system rather than as a diagnostic afterthought. The framework has been implemented end to end and evaluated on two public datasets from different "
"sectors, and the work makes five contributions."),
("bullet","A comparative evaluation of logistic regression, random forest, and XGBoost under one identical training protocol on two public datasets spanning retail "
"banking and subscription streaming, so that conclusions about model behaviour do not rest on a single domain and the comparison measures the models rather than the "
"diligence with which each was tuned."),
("bullet","A dual-axis assessment protocol that scores models on discrimination and calibration as well as on the stability and fidelity of the explanations they "
"support, together with a measurement of what opacity costs on each axis rather than an assertion that it costs something."),
("bullet","An explanation-to-action taxonomy, held as an editable rule table rather than as code, that maps SHAP-identified churn drivers onto retention interventions "
"with assigned business owners and a priority weighted by the value at stake."),
("bullet","A decision-support dashboard, aimed at non-technical CRM users, that presents churn probability, the leading drivers of that probability, and a recommended "
"intervention for each customer, with batch scoring of uploaded customer lists, a versioned model registry, and an audit trail of every score and every override."),
("bullet","An implemented treatment of the ethical obligations that follow from using customer data to drive differential treatment: a fairness audit whose findings are "
"published on the model card, an invariant that no offer is ever made on the basis of a demographic driver, and a human override that is logged and reviewed."),
("body","The remainder of the paper is organised as follows. Section II reviews prior work on churn prediction, explainable ML, and decision support, and states the "
"research gap. Section III presents the framework. Section IV details the methodology, including datasets, preparation, feature engineering, model selection, and "
"evaluation. Section V develops the explainability and decision-support components. Section VI reports the results. Section VII addresses ethical and practical "
"considerations. Section VIII discusses limitations and future work, and Section IX concludes."),

("h1","Related Work"),
("h2","Machine Learning for Churn Prediction"),
("body","Churn prediction has a long history in analytical CRM. Early surveys already framed it as a classification problem over behavioural and contractual attributes "
"and noted the difficulty of moving from prediction to management action {{hadden}}. Verbeke et al. broadened the evaluation question by showing that the model "
"which maximises statistical accuracy is not necessarily the model that maximises campaign profit, an observation that anticipates much of the present argument "
"about the insufficiency of accuracy-centric evaluation {{verbeke}}. Vafeiadis et al. benchmarked a set of standard classifiers on telecommunications data and "
"found boosted ensembles superior to single models, a result replicated many times since {{vafeiadis}}. Ahmad et al. reached similar conclusions at industrial "
"scale, training tree ensembles on operator data covering millions of subscribers and reporting area under the receiver operating characteristic curve values "
"above 0.93 {{ahmad}}."),
("body","Two methodological strands within this literature matter for the present work. The first concerns model structure. De Caigny et al. proposed a hybrid of "
"logistic regression and decision trees precisely because end users found pure ensembles unintelligible, showing that the interpretability concern has been "
"visible inside the churn literature for some time {{decaigny}}. The second concerns features. Alboukaey et al. demonstrated that dynamic behavioural features "
"computed over daily windows outperform static monthly aggregates in mobile telecommunications, which motivates the inclusion of recency and frequency features "
"in the present design {{alboukaey}}. Class imbalance is a recurring obstacle across the strand: churners are usually a small minority of records, and Burez and "
"Van den Poel showed that sampling strategy affects reported performance as much as classifier choice does {{burez}}. The synthetic minority over-sampling "
"technique (SMOTE) of Chawla et al. remains the most common remedy {{chawla}}."),
("body","A recent systematic review by Imani et al., covering 240 studies published between 2020 and 2024, offers a useful summary of where the field now stands: "
"gradient boosting dominates on tabular churn data, deep learning delivers at best marginal gains outside sequential or textual inputs, and the great majority of "
"studies still evaluate on a single dataset from a single sector {{imani}}. The review is also candid about what the literature neglects, listing interpretability, "
"class imbalance handling, and deployment realism among the most persistent gaps. Read critically, the accumulated evidence supports a clear conclusion. The "
"accuracy question is largely settled, and the open problems are comparative generalisation across domains and the usability of model outputs, which are exactly "
"the problems this project takes up."),
("h2","Explainable Artificial Intelligence"),
("body","XAI research divides into intrinsically interpretable models, whose structure can be read directly, and post-hoc methods, which explain a trained model from "
"the outside {{adadi,guidotti}}. Among post-hoc methods, two dominate applied work. LIME fits a sparse linear surrogate to the model's behaviour in the "
"neighbourhood of a single instance, producing a local explanation that is intuitive but sensitive to the sampling used to build the neighbourhood {{ribeiro}}. "
"SHAP grounds attribution in cooperative game theory, assigning each feature its Shapley value, and is unique in satisfying local accuracy, missingness, and "
"consistency simultaneously {{lundberg}}. For tree ensembles, the TreeExplainer algorithm computes exact Shapley values in polynomial time, which makes SHAP "
"practical for the model classes that dominate churn prediction {{lundberg2020}}."),
("body","The two methods are complementary rather than interchangeable. SHAP offers axiomatic guarantees and consistent global summaries but assumes feature "
"independence in its common approximations, which can distribute credit misleadingly across correlated features. LIME is model-agnostic and cheap for "
"single instances but is known to produce unstable explanations when the perturbation process is re-run. Rudin's critique cuts deeper: post-hoc explanations "
"describe the model, not the world, and can lend unwarranted authority to a flawed predictor {{rudin}}. The design consequence adopted in this project is "
"threefold. A transparent baseline model is retained throughout as a reference point, SHAP explanations are cross-checked against LIME on a common sample, and "
"explanations are audited against domain knowledge before being exposed to business users. Recent applied studies, such as the multi-model ensemble analysis of "
"El Attar and El-Hajj, show SHAP being used to rank churn drivers on telecommunications data, but the interpretation is offered to the reader as evidence of "
"model plausibility rather than operationalised for retention staff {{elattar}}."),
("h2","Decision Support and Profit-Aware Retention"),
("body","A separate research strand asks what a churn model is for. Verbraken et al. formalised the expected maximum profit criterion, which evaluates a classifier by "
"the profit of the retention campaign it induces rather than by its error rate {{verbraken}}. Höppner et al. pushed the same logic into model training by "
"deriving profit-driven decision trees whose split criterion is monetary rather than statistical {{hoppner}}. Lemmens and Gupta showed empirically that targeting "
"the customers whose retention creates the most value differs from targeting those most likely to churn {{lemmens}}. Uplift modelling generalises the point by "
"estimating the causal effect of an intervention on each customer, so that campaigns are aimed where they change behaviour rather than where risk is merely "
"high {{devriendt}}."),
("body","This strand supplies the economic rationale for a decision-support layer, but it has developed almost independently of the XAI strand. Profit-aware papers "
"rarely explain individual predictions, and XAI papers rarely cost their recommendations. The framework presented here sits deliberately at the intersection: "
"Shapley attributions supply the reasons, and an intervention taxonomy with business ownership supplies the economically motivated response."),
("h2","Research Gap"),
("body","Three gaps emerge from the review. First, the accuracy-interpretability relationship in churn prediction is usually presented as a trade-off to be accepted "
"rather than an interaction to be measured; studies seldom report how much discrimination is sacrificed, if any, when an interpretable pipeline is required, and "
"seldom quantify explanation stability at all. Second, no widely reported study translates per-customer explanation outputs into a structured, auditable set of "
"retention actions for non-technical stakeholders; the explanation is treated as the end of the analysis rather than the beginning of the decision. Third, "
"cross-domain validation is rare, leaving open the question of whether churn drivers identified in one sector transfer to another {{imani}}. The framework "
"described in the following sections addresses all three directly: it measures discrimination and explanation quality jointly and reports both, it operationalises "
"explanations through an intervention taxonomy and a working dashboard, and it evaluates across two sectors with entirely different feature vocabularies."),

("h1","Proposed Framework"),
("body","The framework is organised as a pipeline of five layers, illustrated in Fig. 1, each of which consumes the outputs of the previous one. The data layer "
"acquires and prepares the datasets described in Section IV. The feature layer organises predictors into behavioural, transactional, contractual, engagement, and "
"demographic categories, giving every downstream explanation a vocabulary that business users already speak, and marking the one category on which no offer may be "
"made. The model layer trains the three classifiers and selects, per dataset, the model that offers the best joint profile of discrimination, calibration, and "
"explanation quality. The explanation layer computes SHAP values for every scored customer and validates them against LIME on a fixed audit sample. The decision "
"layer maps explanations onto retention interventions and presents the result through a dashboard designed for CRM practitioners."),
("body","Three design principles run through the pipeline. The first is that interpretability is a requirement, not a preference, so every modelling choice is assessed "
"for its effect on the explanation layer as well as on predictive performance. The second is that every automated recommendation must remain open to human "
"revision; the system proposes, and the retention team disposes. The third is that a demographic attribute may enter an explanation but never an offer: suppressing "
"such an attribute from the explanation would make the explanation a lie, while acting on it would make the offer discriminatory. These principles shape concrete "
"choices reported below, including the retention of logistic regression as a permanent baseline and the decision to expose driver categories in business language "
"rather than raw feature names in the user interface."),
("fig","framework"),
("body","The pipeline is realised as one Python code base with two entry points: a modelling package that runs the offline pipeline and writes versioned artefacts, and "
"a web application that imports that package rather than reimplementing it. The feature vocabulary, the calibration mathematics, and the intervention taxonomy "
"therefore have exactly one definition each, so what the dashboard shows a retention manager is by construction what the training run measured and registered."),
("body","The pipeline is also an accountability structure. Every trained model is stored in a versioned registry together with its training data snapshot, identified "
"by a SHA-256 digest, its hyperparameters, its evaluation report, and the explanation and fairness audits described in Sections V and VI, and every score served to "
"the dashboard records the model version that produced it. This bookkeeping is unglamorous but essential: when a retention decision is later questioned, whether by "
"a manager, an auditor, or the customer concerned, the framework can reproduce the prediction, the explanation, and the recommendation exactly as they stood at the "
"time of the decision. The same records support the monitoring regime set out in Section VII, since drift in the served population can be measured against the "
"stored training snapshot."),

("h1","Methodology"),
("h2","Datasets"),
("body","Two publicly available, labelled datasets were used, drawn from sectors with different contractual dynamics and entirely different feature vocabularies so "
"that model behaviour could be examined across domains rather than within a single benchmark. Their characteristics are summarised in Table I. The banking dataset "
"records 165,034 retail banking clients with credit score, country, gender, age, tenure, account balance, number of products held, card holding, an activity flag, "
"and estimated salary; 21.2% have closed their account, which is the class imbalance the framework is built to handle. The streaming dataset records 5,000 "
"subscribers of a video-on-demand service with age, gender, subscription tier, hours watched, days since last login, region, device, monthly fee, payment method, "
"number of profiles, average daily viewing time, and favourite genre; 50.3% have cancelled. A third, unlabelled banking file of 110,023 records is used to "
"demonstrate batch scoring through the dashboard, which is the realistic operational case: a customer list arrives without the answer attached."),
("body","A third sector was intended and is not reported, and the reason is worth stating rather than concealing. The e-commerce file obtained for the study carries no "
"churn label, so it supports no supervised model. The obvious repair, defining churn as the absence of a purchase within some window, is a trap: the file's "
"engagement score correlates at r = −0.85 with days since last purchase, so a model retaining both would post a near-perfect area under the curve that is pure "
"leakage; and with both removed, the remaining eleven numeric predictors correlate with the derived label at |r| ≤ 0.03, which is a coin flip. Fabricating a third "
"domain is worse than reporting two, so the cross-domain claim in this paper rests on banking and streaming. A labelled e-commerce file would enter the pipeline as "
"a single new dataset declaration whenever one becomes available."),
("body","Both files are anonymised and distributed for research use, which keeps the ethical footprint of the study small. Surname is nevertheless dropped from the "
"banking data rather than merely left unused: it is a direct identifier and a proxy for ethnicity and nationality, and no model in a retention system has any "
"business reading one. The streaming figures reported in Section VI should be read with suspicion for reasons given there; the banking figures are the ones by "
"which the framework should be judged."),
("table","datasets"),
("h2","Data Preparation"),
("body","Preparation follows an identical protocol on each dataset so that cross-domain comparisons are not confounded by differing preprocessing. Records with "
"duplicate identifiers are removed. Continuous fields with missing values are imputed with the median; categorical fields are given an explicit Missing level rather "
"than being silently filled, so that absence remains visible to the explanation layer. Categorical predictors are one-hot encoded. Continuous predictors are scaled "
"to the unit interval with min-max normalisation, which logistic regression requires for stable coefficient estimation and which does not harm tree-based models. "
"Predictors with near-zero variance are dropped, as is one member of any pair whose absolute correlation exceeds 0.9; on the banking data this removed two derived "
"predictors, balance per product and a zero-balance flag, each of which duplicated information already carried by the account balance. Each dataset is then split "
"into training and test partitions in an 80/20 ratio, stratified on the churn label."),
("body","Class imbalance is addressed with SMOTE {{chawla}}, applied under two constraints that the literature identifies as necessary for honest evaluation "
"{{burez}}. Synthetic examples are generated only from training data, never from test data, and the oversampler sits inside the cross-validation pipeline so that "
"it is fitted within each fold rather than before the split; no synthetic point derived from a validation instance can therefore leak into the corresponding "
"training set. Test partitions retain their natural class distribution throughout, since performance claims are only credible against the imbalance the model will "
"face in production."),
("body","The banking results reported below were produced on a stratified 20,000-record subsample of the 165,034 available, preserving the 21.2% positive rate. The "
"reason is computational rather than statistical: the random forest grid alone requires 160 forest fits, and the full file takes hours per model. The subsample is "
"recorded in the model artefact alongside the digest of the source file, so the reported figures state exactly what they were computed on."),
("h2","Feature Engineering"),
("body","Predictors are organised into five categories, which serve both as an engineering checklist and, later, as the vocabulary of the explanation layer and the "
"matching keys of the decision layer."),
("bullet","Behavioural features: login or session frequency, product usage rate, breadth of feature adoption, and recency of use, computed over recent windows where "
"timestamps permit."),
("bullet","Transactional features: average monthly spend, payment method, billing cycle, subscription fee, and outstanding balance."),
("bullet","Contractual features: contract or tier, tenure, renewal history, product count, and the presence of value-added services."),
("bullet","Engagement features: complaint frequency, satisfaction proxies where available, and response to past promotional contact."),
("bullet","Demographic features: age, gender, and geography. These are permitted as predictors and as explanations, and are excluded by construction from anything that "
"triggers a differential offer."),
("body","Derived features follow the evidence on temporal dynamics {{alboukaey}}: ratio and recency variables are added where the raw fields allow. The banking data "
"gains balance against salary, products taken up per year, and the share of adult life spent as a customer; the streaming data gains watch hours per profile, fee "
"per profile, and a dormancy flag. Feature selection is otherwise kept conservative, for the reason given above: strongly correlated features both destabilise "
"logistic regression coefficients and dilute Shapley attributions across duplicates {{lundberg2020}}. No aggressive automated selection is applied, because the "
"explanation layer, not a selection algorithm, is where the framework interrogates feature relevance."),
("h2","Model Selection and Justification"),
("body","Three classifiers are trained on every dataset. They were chosen to form a ladder of increasing representational power with decreasing native transparency, "
"which is precisely the trade-off the study is designed to measure."),
("body","Logistic regression is the baseline. It models the churn probability as shown in (1), where x is the feature vector, β the coefficient vector, and "
"β subscript zero the intercept."),
("eq", [("p","i"),("(","n"),("x","i"),(") = 1 / (1 + exp(−(β","n"),("0","sub"),(" + β","n"),("T","sup"),("x","i"),(")))","n")]),
("body","Its advantages are exact interpretability, since each coefficient is a log-odds contribution, together with fast training, stable behaviour on modest "
"samples, and well-calibrated probabilities. Its limitation is the linearity assumption: interactions and threshold effects, which are common in churn data, "
"must be hand-crafted or are missed. It is retained not despite this simplicity but because of it, as the reference against which the cost of opacity is priced."),
("body","Random forest aggregates several hundred decorrelated decision trees grown on bootstrap samples with random feature subsets {{breiman}}. It captures "
"non-linearities and interactions without manual engineering, is robust to outliers and to the mixed feature types typical of CRM data, and its bagged "
"structure resists overfitting. Its drawbacks are the loss of direct interpretability, a tendency to dilute importance across correlated features, and "
"probability estimates that often require recalibration."),
("body","XGBoost implements regularised gradient boosting, building trees sequentially so that each corrects the residual errors of its predecessors, with explicit "
"penalties on tree complexity {{chen}}. It is the strongest performer on tabular churn benchmarks {{vafeiadis,ahmad,imani}} and handles imbalance through "
"instance weighting in addition to resampling. Its costs are sensitivity to hyperparameters, a greater risk of overfitting small datasets than bagging, and "
"the same native opacity as any large ensemble."),
("body","Deep neural architectures were considered and set aside. The systematic evidence indicates that on tabular data of the size used here they seldom beat "
"tuned gradient boosting, while demanding more data, more tuning, and heavier explanation machinery {{imani}}. All three retained models are compatible with "
"exact or efficient Shapley computation, logistic regression trivially and the two ensembles through TreeExplainer {{lundberg2020}}, which keeps the "
"explanation layer computationally honest."),
("h2","Training Protocol and Hyperparameter Optimisation"),
("body","Every model runs the same seven stages, so that the comparison measures the models and not the effort spent on each. The data are prepared as described "
"above; hyperparameters are tuned by stratified ten-fold cross-validation on the training partition, scored by average precision, with SMOTE applied inside each "
"fold; probabilities are calibrated; an operating threshold is chosen; the model is refitted and evaluated once; the explanations are audited; and the artefact is "
"registered. Logistic regression is tuned over the inverse regularisation strength under an L2 penalty across fourteen candidates. Random forest is tuned by grid "
"search over the number of estimators, maximum depth, minimum samples per split, and maximum features, across sixteen candidates and therefore 160 forest fits. "
"XGBoost, whose parameter space is too large for exhaustive search, is tuned by Bayesian optimisation with the Optuna framework and a tree-structured Parzen "
"estimator over learning rate, depth, subsampling ratios, regularisation, and the number of boosting rounds, across twenty-five trials {{akiba}}."),
("body","Probability outputs are then calibrated by isotonic regression fitted on out-of-fold probabilities from a five-fold split of the training partition. The "
"decision layer consumes probabilities rather than labels, and a miscalibrated 0.8 is operationally misleading; isotonic regression is monotone, so it corrects "
"the probabilities without disturbing the Shapley ranking that the decision layer reads."),
("body","Classification requires an operating threshold as well as a probability, and the choice is a business decision disguised as a technical one. Rather than "
"defaulting to 0.5, the threshold is selected on the validation folds to maximise F1-score subject to a minimum precision, set here to 0.60, that in practice would "
"be agreed with the retention budget holder, since precision determines how much of the campaign budget is spent on customers who were never going to leave. The "
"selected threshold is stored with the model and reported with every score, so that published performance figures correspond to the configuration the decision "
"layer actually uses. Section VI quantifies what this single choice is worth."),
("body","The implementation uses the standard Python scientific stack. All random seeds are fixed at 42 and recorded, along with the library versions and the SHA-256 "
"digest of the source file, in each model artefact, so that a reported figure can be traced to the exact data and code that produced it."),
("h2","Evaluation Metrics"),
("body","Accuracy alone is uninformative under imbalance: a classifier that never predicts churn is 79% accurate on the banking data. The evaluation therefore "
"reports a suite of complementary metrics. Precision, defined in (2), measures the proportion of predicted churners who actually churn, and governs how much "
"retention budget is wasted on customers who were never leaving. Recall, defined in (3), measures the proportion of actual churners the model catches, and governs "
"how much revenue walks out unnoticed. The F1-score, defined in (4), is their harmonic mean and is reported as a single-number balance of the two."),
("eq", [("Precision = TP / (TP + FP)","n")]),
("eq", [("Recall = TP / (TP + FN)","n")]),
("eq", [("F","i"),("1","sub"),(" = 2 · Precision · Recall / (Precision + Recall)","n")]),
("body","Here TP, FP, and FN denote true positives, false positives, and false negatives respectively. Threshold-free discrimination is reported as the area under "
"the receiver operating characteristic curve (ROC-AUC). Because ROC-AUC can flatter models under heavy imbalance, the Matthews correlation coefficient (MCC) "
"is reported alongside it, following the evidence of Chicco and Jurman that MCC is the more conservative summary of a confusion matrix {{chicco}}. Probability "
"calibration is assessed with the Brier score. Finally, because the point of the system is economic, the evaluation includes a profit-oriented reading in the "
"spirit of the expected maximum profit criterion, valuing the confusion matrix at the operating threshold the decision layer uses {{verbraken}}. The unit "
"economics assumed for that reading, 100 for a customer retained, 15 for an offer wasted, and 200 for a customer lost, are deliberate placeholders: they are the "
"first thing an adopting firm must replace with its own numbers, because they, and not the model, decide where the threshold lands. Explanation quality is "
"assessed against the measures set out in Section V and reported alongside these predictive metrics."),

("h1","Explainability and Decision Support"),
("h2","Interpreting Shapley Explanations"),
("body","SHAP expresses every prediction as an additive attribution, as shown in (5), where g is the explanation model, z′ the simplified feature presence "
"vector, M the number of features, φ subscript zero the base value equal to the mean model output, and each φ subscript j the Shapley value of "
"feature j {{lundberg}}."),
("eq", [("g","i"),("(","n"),("z","i"),("′) = φ","n"),("0","sub"),(" + Σ","n"),("j","isub"),(" φ","n"),("j","isub"),(" ","n"),("z","i"),("′","n"),("j","isub")]),
("body","Three views of these attributions are produced for the tree ensembles with TreeExplainer {{lundberg2020}}. Global feature importance, computed as mean "
"absolute Shapley value, tells the business which drivers dominate churn across the whole customer base and is the natural input to strategic decisions such "
"as a pricing review. Directional summaries add sign, showing for instance that short tenure raises churn risk while long tenure suppresses it. "
"Per-customer decompositions break one individual's risk estimate into named contributions, and it is this local view that the decision layer consumes. Every "
"attribution is relabelled from the encoded column name into business language before it leaves the modelling package, so that the dashboard shows a retention "
"manager Years as a customer rather than num__Tenure. Interpretation is disciplined by two rules. Attributions are read as descriptions of model behaviour, not as "
"causal claims about customers, a distinction Rudin's critique makes unavoidable {{rudin}}; and any driver whose direction contradicts domain knowledge is "
"escalated for data-quality review before the model is trusted."),
("h2","Cross-Validation with Local Surrogate Models"),
("body","Because post-hoc explanations can be fragile, SHAP outputs are audited against LIME on a fixed sample of 100 test-set predictions per model, stratified "
"across the risk spectrum {{ribeiro}}. For each sampled customer the top five features by absolute attribution are extracted from both methods and compared on "
"three measures: set overlap, Jaccard similarity, and rank agreement. LIME is additionally re-run with different random states on the same records, and the "
"agreement between its own runs is recorded as a stability score, since an explainer that disagrees with itself cannot arbitrate anything. High agreement raises "
"confidence that the explanation reflects the model rather than the idiosyncrasies of one explainer; systematic disagreement localises the features whose "
"attributions should not be shown to business users without a caveat. Features on which the two methods disagree in more than half of the records where SHAP "
"ranks them highly are recorded in the artefact as contested, and any recommendation resting on one of them carries a visible warning in the dashboard."),
("h2","From Explanations to Retention Actions"),
("body","The step that distinguishes this framework is the mapping from explanation to intervention. The three strongest SHAP drivers for a customer are grouped "
"into the feature categories of Section IV and matched against a retention intervention taxonomy developed with reference to the retention-marketing literature "
"{{lemmens,verbeke}}. Table II sets out a representative extract of the eighteen rules the implementation carries. Rules match either a specific feature or a "
"whole category, are evaluated in order so that specific rules precede general ones, and the first rule matching an actionable driver produces the recommendation. "
"A customer whose risk is driven by dormancy is routed to marketing for a win-back sequence; one driven by a single product holding is routed to sales for a "
"cross-sell; one driven by a service complaint is routed to service recovery within 48 hours."),
("body","Two mechanisms turn the resulting list into a work queue rather than a ranking. First, each rule carries a weight, which is combined with the customer's "
"calibrated probability band to produce a priority of P1 to P3. Second, priority is scaled by the value at stake, measured against the median value in the training "
"data and bounded to a multiplier between 0.6 and 1.6, because targeting the customers whose retention creates the most value is not the same as targeting those "
"most likely to leave, and a queue sorted on probability alone quietly assumes that it is {{lemmens}}. The taxonomy is stored as an editable JSON rule table rather "
"than as code, is re-read whenever it changes on disk, and is published in full in the dashboard, so that retention managers can adjust it as offers change without "
"a redeployment and without a developer."),
("body","One rule is an invariant rather than a preference. If a customer's leading driver is demographic, no automated offer is made on that basis: the "
"recommendation falls through to the strongest actionable driver, and the customer is referred to a retention manager if none exists. The explanation still shows "
"the demographic driver, because hiding it would misrepresent the model, but the offer never rests on it. This behaviour is enforced in the decision layer and "
"covered by a regression test, so that it cannot be removed by accident."),
("table","interventions"),
("h2","Decision-Support Dashboard"),
("body","The dashboard is implemented as a Django application that imports the modelling package directly rather than reimplementing any part of it. A CRM user "
"uploads a customer list as a comma-separated file and chooses a registered model; the application returns, for each customer, the calibrated churn probability "
"expressed as a banded score, the three strongest churn drivers stated in category language rather than raw feature names, and the recommended intervention with "
"its owner and priority. Batch summaries show the distribution of risk across the uploaded base, the queue by priority, and the aggregate driver profile, which "
"supports campaign-level planning as well as case-level action. Nothing in the interface requires statistical literacy: the design assumes a user who knows the "
"customers and the offers, not the models. An export function returns the scored list for ingestion into an existing CRM, carrying the reasons and the model "
"version and not merely the score, and a JSON endpoint offers the same payload to other systems. Every screen carries the model version, the operating threshold, "
"and the scoring date, so that a decision can be traced to the model that informed it."),
("body","Fig. 2 shows the batch summary for a 400-record slice of the unlabelled banking file scored by the recommended model. Of those customers 85, or 21.2% of the "
"uploaded base, fall above the operating threshold; 29 are assigned P1 and 33 P2, leaving 338 to be monitored rather than contacted. Mean calibrated risk across "
"the base is 0.20. The batch-level driver profile attributes 43% of total attribution to contract and products, 41% to demographic attributes, 15% to usage and "
"activity, and 1% to money and payments, which is a campaign-level finding in its own right: where one category dominates, the answer is usually a single "
"structural change rather than a hundred individual calls."),
("figwide","dashsummary"),
("body","Fig. 3 shows the queue itself. Each row carries the customer identifier, the risk band, the three strongest drivers with their categories, the recommended "
"action, the owning team, and the priority. Two annotations in that figure are the visible surface of mechanisms described above. A driver tagged not used for "
"offers is demographic, and the accompanying note states that the recommendation rests instead on the strongest driver the business can legitimately act on. A "
"driver tagged disputed is one on which SHAP and LIME disagreed during the audit, and the accompanying note asks the user to confirm before acting. In the batch "
"shown, 215 of the 400 explanations carry at least one such caveat, which is not a defect of the display but an honest report of what the audit found."),
("figwide","dashqueue"),
("body","The system is advisory throughout. Any recommendation may be overridden, an override requires a reason, and the reason, the person, and the timestamp are "
"written to an audit log that is read-only in the administrative interface, since evidence that can be edited after the fact is not evidence. The overview screen "
"displays the override rate, because an override rate of zero is not a triumph: it is the signature of automation bias, the tendency to defer to the system "
"precisely because it is a system."),

("h1","Results"),
("h2","Predictive Performance"),
("body","Table III reports the single evaluation of each model on the test partition it never saw during preparation, tuning, calibration, or threshold selection. "
"Fig. 4(a) shows the corresponding ROC curves for the banking models. On the banking data the ordering matches the literature: XGBoost leads on every threshold-free "
"measure, with ROC-AUC 0.883, MCC 0.570, and F1 0.665, followed closely by the random forest at 0.881, 0.543, and 0.644, with logistic regression at 0.831, 0.468, "
"and 0.541. The accuracy column is instructive precisely because it is uninformative: all three models sit between 0.84 and 0.85, a range of one percentage point, "
"while MCC spreads across ten. A study reporting accuracy alone would conclude that the choice of model does not matter here, and it would be wrong."),
("fig","roccal"),
("tablewide","performance"),
("body","The streaming results should be read as a warning rather than as a result. ROC-AUC of 0.9999 and MCC of 0.984 are not how churn behaves in the wild, and the "
"explanation is in the data rather than in the models: a depth-five decision tree fitted to just three of the file's columns, average daily viewing, days since last "
"login, and hours watched, recovers 90% of the label under five-fold cross-validation. The models are rediscovering the rule that generated the file, not predicting "
"a cancellation. The dataset remains useful, because it exercises every layer of the framework on a second domain with a different feature vocabulary, which is what "
"the cross-domain design needs it for, and because its near-balanced classes are a genuine counterweight to the banking data. But the banking figures are the ones "
"by which the framework should be judged, and this caveat is repeated on the streaming model cards in the dashboard, where a reader might otherwise see 0.99 and "
"believe it."),
("h2","Calibration and the Operating Threshold"),
("body","Fig. 4(b) shows the reliability of the recommended banking model before and after calibration. The raw gradient-boosted output is badly overconfident across "
"the whole range; isotonic regression pulls the curve onto the diagonal and improves the Brier score from 0.138 to 0.103 on the out-of-fold probabilities, with a "
"test-set Brier of 0.099. Since the decision layer bands probabilities into risk tiers and scales priority by them, this correction is not cosmetic: it is what "
"makes a displayed 0.72 mean roughly what a retention manager will take it to mean."),
("body","Fig. 5 prices the threshold decision. Holding the model fixed and sweeping the operating threshold across the full range, campaign value at the selected "
"threshold of 0.329 is +1.56 per customer, while at the conventional default of 0.5 it is −6.52: a swing of 8.08 per customer, on placeholder economics, produced "
"entirely by a choice the model does not make. The curve also shows why the precision floor matters. Value rises monotonically as the threshold falls, because under "
"the assumed economics a missed churner costs 200 and a wasted offer costs 15; without a precision constraint the optimiser would contact almost everyone, which is "
"a defensible strategy only if those numbers are right. The floor is the mechanism by which a budget holder's judgement enters the model, and it is stated rather "
"than buried."),
("fig","threshold"),
("h2","Explanation Quality and the Cost of Opacity"),
("body","Table IV reports the second assessment axis, and Fig. 6 plots the two axes against each other. On the banking data the trade-off the literature usually "
"asserts is visible and monotone: as discrimination improves across the ladder, agreement between the two explainers falls. Top-five overlap between SHAP and LIME "
"declines from 0.840 for logistic regression to 0.716 for the random forest and 0.664 for XGBoost, and rank agreement, the stricter measure, collapses from 0.720 "
"to 0.486 to 0.300. Stated as a price, the 0.102 of MCC that gradient boosting buys over the transparent baseline costs 0.176 of explanation overlap and 0.420 of "
"rank agreement. That is the number the accuracy-interpretability debate has generally lacked."),
("fig","joint"),
("tablewide","audit"),
("body","The streaming panel of Fig. 6 shows that this is a property of a particular data and model pairing rather than a law. There XGBoost attains both the highest "
"MCC and the highest explanation agreement of the three, at 0.984 and 0.794, while the random forest is worst on the explanation axis at 0.722. Where the underlying "
"relationship is a clean threshold rule, a well-regularised booster can recover it in a form that two different explainers describe the same way. The generalisable "
"claim is therefore not that complexity always costs interpretability, but that the cost varies, is measurable, and should be measured rather than assumed."),
("body","The framework converts these two axes into a recommendation under a deliberately conservative rule: a model whose explanations fail the audit is disqualified "
"regardless of its discrimination, and an ensemble that beats the transparent baseline by less than one point of MCC loses to it, because an unexplainable model has "
"to earn its opacity. Under that rule XGBoost was recommended on both datasets, beating the logistic baseline by 0.102 MCC on banking and 0.199 on streaming. Had "
"the banking margin been a tenth of that, the baseline would have been recommended instead, and the recommendation records that reasoning rather than merely its "
"conclusion."),
("body","The audit also names the features on which the two explainers disagree. For the recommended banking model these are estimated salary, products taken up per "
"year, credit score, account balance, years as a customer, and country, six of the sixteen encoded predictors, with disagreement rates between 0.89 and 1.00 on the "
"records where SHAP ranks them highly. Two of these, account balance and years as a customer, are drivers on which the taxonomy would otherwise act, which is why "
"the dashboard flags them rather than suppressing them."),
("h2","What the Models Read"),
("body","Fig. 7 shows the global Shapley ranking for the recommended banking model. Age is the strongest driver in the whole model, at a mean absolute Shapley value "
"of 1.19, marginally ahead of the number of products held at 1.14 and well ahead of the activity flag at 0.59; gender and country appear fifth and sixth. Three of "
"the six leading drivers of the model are therefore demographic. This is what makes the invariant of Section V a practical matter rather than a principled one: on "
"this data, a system that acted on its strongest drivers would be making offers on the basis of age, sex, and nationality in a substantial fraction of cases."),
("fig","importance"),
("body","The streaming model reads an entirely different vocabulary. Its three leading drivers are average daily viewing at 3.47, hours watched at 3.32, and days since "
"last login at 3.03, all behavioural, with monthly fee fourth. No demographic attribute appears near the top. The same taxonomy nevertheless routes both populations "
"without modification: the banking customers reach sales and customer success through contract and product rules, and the streaming customers reach marketing "
"through dormancy and usage rules. That the decision layer transfers across two domains with no shared feature names is the clearest evidence available here for "
"the cross-domain claim."),
("h2","Fairness Audit"),
("body","Table V and Fig. 8 report the fairness audit of the recommended model on each dataset. On the banking data the audit fails on all three declared sensitive "
"attributes. Selection-rate ratios are 0.50 for gender, 0.36 for country, and 0.07 for age band, against a four-fifths convention of 0.80, and true-positive-rate "
"gaps are 0.15, 0.29, and 0.67 respectively. The audit additionally flags three demographic attributes, age, gender, and country, as appearing among the model's "
"leading drivers."),
("table","fairness"),
("fig","fairness"),
("body","Part of this disparity reflects the data rather than the model. Base churn rates differ sharply between groups: 37.6% of German clients in the test partition "
"had closed their account against 16.3% of French clients, and 54.1% of clients aged 45 to 59 against 7.3% of those under 30. A model that ignored those differences "
"would be a worse model. But the operational consequence stands regardless of its cause: a system that flags 5% of under-thirties and 70% of clients aged 45 to 59 "
"is distributing retention spending very unequally, and the group that receives no offer receives no offer whether the reason is bias or base rate. The framework's "
"answer is neither to suppress the finding nor to accept it silently. The audit is published on the model card in the dashboard, the demographic invariant prevents "
"the disparity from being converted directly into differential offers, and the decision is escalated to a human."),
("body","The streaming model passes the same audit on all three of its sensitive attributes, with selection-rate ratios of 0.92 for gender, 0.87 for region, and 0.93 "
"for age band, and true-positive-rate gaps below 0.03. The contrast is informative: the fairness properties of a churn system are a property of the data it is "
"trained on at least as much as of the algorithm applied to it, which is an argument for auditing every deployment rather than certifying a method once."),
("h2","Cost and Reproducibility"),
("body","Training the full ladder on the 20,000-record banking sample took 31 seconds for logistic regression, 188 seconds for XGBoost, and 1,344 seconds for the "
"random forest, whose exhaustive grid dominates the budget; the streaming runs took 61, 92, and 171 seconds respectively. That the Bayesian search over a larger "
"space is seven times faster than the grid over a smaller one is a practical argument for the former at scale. Every run writes an artefact carrying the fitted "
"pipeline, the calibrators, the hyperparameters, the evaluation report, both audits, the library versions, the seed, and the SHA-256 digest of the source file, and "
"registers it under a timestamped version. The figures in this section were regenerated from those artefacts rather than transcribed, by reproducing the "
"deterministic test partition and re-scoring it."),

("h1","Ethical and Practical Considerations"),
("body","A system that uses personal data to decide who receives retention offers carries obligations beyond predictive performance. Privacy comes first. The "
"study itself uses anonymised public datasets, but the framework is designed for production use, so it assumes pseudonymised identifiers, data minimisation "
"in the feature set, and role-based access to the dashboard; no screen showing customer risk is reachable without authentication, and that property is covered by a "
"test rather than by an assurance. A configuration flag retains the score, the drivers, and the recommendation while discarding the personal data behind them, for "
"deployments where the audit trail is required but the record is not. The dashboard loads no external asset, charts being rendered server-side and embedded, so a "
"page displaying customer risk reports to nobody. Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), customers have a qualified right to "
"meaningful information about automated decisions that significantly affect them, and the per-customer explanations the framework already produces are the "
"natural mechanism for honouring it {{goodman}}."),
("body","Purpose limitation deserves separate mention. Data collected to operate a service is being reused here to predict and influence customer behaviour, and "
"that reuse must be covered by the lawful basis under which the data were gathered and disclosed in the privacy notice customers actually receive. The feature "
"set is reviewed against this test before training: variables whose collection purpose is remote from retention, or whose presence a reasonable customer would "
"find surprising, are excluded even when they carry predictive signal. Surname is the concrete case in this study. Retention periods apply to the modelling data as "
"they do to the operational data from which it derives, and scored lists exported from the dashboard inherit the access controls of the CRM system they enter."),
("body","Fairness requires equal attention, and the audit reported in Section VI shows why an audit with no consequences would be worthless. Churn models trained on "
"historical data can encode historical inequities, and features such as geography or salary can proxy for protected attributes {{mehrabi}}. The framework therefore "
"compares selection and error rates across every declared sensitive attribute, applies the four-fifths convention, inspects Shapley attributions for proxy "
"behaviour, and publishes what it finds on the model card rather than in an appendix. Where it found real disparities on the banking data, it said so. The "
"distributional question specific to retention then follows: if offers flow only to customers the model flags, systematically unflagged groups quietly receive "
"worse treatment. Publishing the intervention taxonomy, enforcing the demographic invariant, and keeping a human review step in the loop are partial but practical "
"safeguards. Finally, the system is advisory by design. Retention staff can override any recommendation, overrides are logged with a reason and an author, and the "
"log is reviewed both to improve the model and to detect automation bias."),
("body","Practical constraints are acknowledged with the same directness. Customer behaviour drifts, so deployed models require scheduled retraining and monitoring "
"of both performance and calibration against the stored training snapshot. Explanation computation adds latency and cost at scoring time, which the design contains "
"by using TreeExplainer and by precomputing explanations during batch scoring rather than on page load. The rule table that maps drivers to interventions embodies "
"commercial judgement that will differ between firms, and is exposed for exactly that reason."),

("h1","Limitations and Future Work"),
("body","The work has limits that should be stated plainly. Cross-domain transfer is evidenced across two sectors rather than three, for the reason given in "
"Section IV, and both datasets are public files rather than proprietary customer records; conclusions therefore need confirmation on operational data before they "
"can guide practice. The streaming label is synthetic, as Section VI demonstrates, so the near-perfect scores on that dataset measure recovery of a generating rule "
"and not prediction of a cancellation. The banking results were produced on a 20,000-record stratified subsample rather than the full 165,034, for reasons of "
"compute; the subsample preserves the class balance but a full-file run remains the stronger evidence. All results come from a single seed, so the reported "
"differences between models are not accompanied by a sampling distribution. SMOTE generates synthetic minority examples by interpolation, and although it is "
"confined to training folds, it can still smooth over rare but genuine churn patterns {{burez}}."),
("body","The explanation and decision layers carry their own limits. Shapley attributions describe the model rather than the customer, so the retention actions they "
"trigger are motivated correlations, not established causes; the framework flags customers and reasons, but it cannot promise that treating the reason will avert "
"the churn. The audit of explanations relies on agreement between two post-hoc methods, which is evidence of robustness rather than proof of fidelity: two methods "
"that agree may both be wrong. The unit economics used in the profit reading are placeholders, and since they determine where the threshold lands, every monetary "
"figure in Section VI should be read as a demonstration of a mechanism rather than as a forecast of a return."),
("body","The intervention taxonomy carries the largest untested assumption of all. It encodes a judgement that a given driver is best answered by a given offer, and "
"that judgement rests on the retention-marketing literature and on face validity rather than on experimental evidence from the firms that would use it. Different "
"sectors price interventions differently, and a mapping that is profitable for a streaming service may be loss-making for a bank. The taxonomy is editable for "
"precisely this reason, but editability transfers the burden rather than discharging it, and the framework's end-to-end value therefore remains a hypothesis until "
"it is measured against realised retention outcomes in the field. The dashboard, similarly, is designed against personas rather than validated with users."),
("body","Each limitation points to further work. The natural methodological extension is uplift modelling, which estimates the effect of an intervention on each "
"customer and would convert the decision layer from risk-based to effect-based targeting {{devriendt}}. Profit-driven training objectives could replace "
"post-hoc profit evaluation, aligning the models themselves with the economics of retention {{hoppner,verbraken}}. A user study with practising CRM staff "
"would test whether the explanations change decisions as intended. On the modelling side, sequence models over event streams merit examination where "
"fine-grained behavioural logs exist {{alboukaey}}, and on the deployment side, a longitudinal field trial measuring realised retention against a control "
"group is the standard the framework should ultimately meet."),

("h1","Conclusion"),
("body","This paper has argued that the useful frontier in churn prediction is no longer accuracy but the distance between a probability and a decision, and it has "
"built and evaluated a framework that closes that distance. Three classifiers of graded complexity were trained under one protocol on two sectors, their Shapley "
"explanations were audited against an independent explainer, and the surviving explanations were translated through an explicit taxonomy into prioritised retention "
"actions delivered in a dashboard built for non-technical staff. Measuring both axes rather than one produced the paper's central quantitative result: on the "
"banking data the 0.102 of MCC that gradient boosting buys over a transparent baseline costs 0.176 of agreement between two explainers and 0.420 of rank agreement, "
"a price that is real, that varies by domain, and that the field has more often asserted than measured. Measuring fairness rather than assuming it produced the "
"second: the recommended banking model fails the four-fifths convention on all three sensitive attributes, which is a fact about the data that a retention system "
"must handle rather than hide. If churn research is to influence retention practice, its outputs must arrive in the language of the people who act on them, "
"together with an honest account of what they cost; the framework presented here is a concrete attempt to make that translation systematic, measurable, and accountable."),

("h5","Acknowledgment"),
("body","The author thanks his project supervisor at the School of Computing, Ulster University, for detailed and constructive feedback on an earlier draft of this "
"paper, which materially improved its scope and rigour."),
]

